WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:01.049
Speaker 1: OK.

00:00:01.049 --> 00:00:10.510
The latest development in the Joe Rogan Spotify
controversy is that the CEO of the Trump affiliated

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:19.680
right wing social media platform Rumble has
offered Rogan 100 million dollars to leave

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.460
Spotify and to bring his show to Rumble.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.199
There's a very short and straightforward Reuters
report about this.

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:36.920
Rogan gets $100 million offer from Trump affiliated
site Rumble Rumble Inc, a YouTube style website

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:43.280
popular among U.S. conservatives, has offered
Joe Rogan $100 million over four years for

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.070
all his shows.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:50.539
Days after the podcaster apologized for using
racial slurs in his content, Rogan is facing

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:54.750
backlash for COVID misinformation on his program
hosted on Spotify.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.079
Neil Young and Joni Mitchell pulled their
content from the platform.

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:03.309
The incidents prompted Spotify to add a content
advisory to any episode featuring discussion

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:08.410
of COVID, as scientists and medical professionals
urged the platform to prevent Rogan from spreading

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.410
falsehoods.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:13.760
So the CEO wrote to Rogan.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:19.820
Chris Pavlovsky is the CEO of Rumble and wrote,
Dear Joe, we stand with you, your guests and

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:23.790
your legion of fans and desire for real conversation.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:28.850
So we'd like to offer you 100 million reasons
to make the world a better place.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:33.220
How about you bring all your shows to rumble
both old and new with no sense censorship

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:36.630
for 100 million bucks over four years?

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.050
This is our chance to save the world.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.980
And yes, this is totally legit.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:47.000
So there's a couple different things here
I think that that are important to talk about.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:55.180
First and foremost, there's a reality that
more than likely Joe Rogan can't just do this

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:58.700
because he's under contract with Spotify.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:05.120
If Spotify pulled his show, they'd probably
still have to pay him.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:08.810
Even if they released him from the contract,
they might still have to give him something

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.160
if he had some other thing.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:14.510
You know, we don't know the exact details
of the contract, so it's like an offer Rumble

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.100
can make.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:20.950
That's very unlikely to become a real thing
because of how these contracts tend to work,

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.620
and I say that without actually having looked
at Joe Rogan's contract.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:29.710
But my my concern here is as follows, and
many of you know that no one I've been on

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.770
Rogan's program twice.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:39.110
And when I was on, no topic was off limits
and I said whatever I wanted to.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:44.569
